Since the condition depends only on $|i|$ and $|j|$, we can iterate over $i \ge 0$ and $j \ge 0$ and multiply by symmetries, or just iterate over all $i, j$.
Given $R \le 10^6$, an $O(R)$ or $O(R \log R)$ solution is acceptable. $O(R^2)$ is too slow ($10^{12}$ operations).
