If we pick $x_i$ units of product $i$, the cost is $\sum_{k=1}^{x_i} (2k-1)P_i = P_i \sum_{k=1}^{x_i} (2k-1) = P_i x_i^2$.
So minimizing $\sum P_i x_i^2$ subject to $\sum x_i = X$ is equivalent to picking the $X$ smallest marginal costs.
The marginal costs are $P_i, 3P_i, 5P_i, \dots$.
Notice that for a fixed $i$, the marginal costs are $P_i, 3P_i, 5P_i, \dots$.
